   REQ-PB-042 notes: Source-grounded core (cited B blocks). AN-04 consolidation: absorbs former REQ-S05-004 (Run the facilitated 90-120-minute TOM workshop mode with agenda, captured contributions and conversion of unresolved items into decisions or actions); its anchors M0147 and acceptance are carried here. The agenda, per-dimension contribution capture, conversion into actions and the no-close-with-unconverted-items rule are master prompt §5 additions (M0147), not playbook content; the 90-120-minute workshop with business owners and conversion into design decisions with owners is source (B0063).
   REQ-PB-058 notes: Shared-benefit allocation rules detailed in master prompt §8. AN-04 consolidation: absorbs former REQ-S08-012 (Prevent double counting through a canonical benefit register, parent/child relationships, shared-benefit groups and contribution allocations so portfolio aggregation counts a shared benefit once); its anchors M0173 and acceptance are carried here. The canonical benefit register, parent/child relationships, shared-benefit groups and contribution allocations are the master prompt §8 mechanism (M0173); the unique owner, baseline, formula and statement/KPI link is source (B0088). Allocation limits: REQ-S08-013; overlap warnings: REQ-S08-014.
   REQ-PB-069 notes: Source-grounded core (cited B blocks). AN-04 consolidation: absorbs former REQ-S11-003 (Track adoption actuals against adoption trajectories and create corrective interventions when gaps appear); its anchors M0216 and acceptance are carried here. Trajectory-based adoption tracking and the exactly-one-intervention rule are master prompt §11 additions (M0216); adoption as an outcome with leading indicators, separate from delivery, is source (B0105). Indicators: REQ-PB-071/072.
