== RAG from trajectory, not task completion
   REQ-PB-063 [SOURCE/SPECIFIED/final DG4] Apply the area-specific T10 RAG logic
      P: Each area computes status by its own rule; outcome RAG never uses task completion; missing data shows Unknown/Stale
      A: A04;A05: an outcome whose tasks are 100% complete but KPI is below trajectory is Red/Amber, not Green; a KPI with no actual shows Unknown
   REQ-PB-064 [SOURCE/SPECIFIED/final DG4] Show a Decisions area Red when an executive decision is overdue
      P: Any open executive decision past its due date turns the Decisions area Red and lists the overdue item
      A: A09: with one open T16 decision due yesterday (Asia/Riyadh), Decisions area is Red and lists it; after the decision is recorded it no longer counts
   REQ-S07-007 [USER/SPECIFIED/final DG4] Compute RAG from the approved expected trajectory with configurable thresholds and never from project task completion
      P: RAG = evaluation of actual versus expected-to-date by polarity using configured thresholds; task completion is not an input
      A: A04;A05: with all tasks complete and actual below the red threshold the KPI is Red; changing the threshold version recomputes RAG
   REQ-S01-005 [ENGINEERING/SPECIFIED/final DG6] Never imply an external operational change happened because a task was marked complete; require verified evidence or a confirmed integration result
      P: Deliverables flagged as external changes carry a separate confirmation state that only reviewed evidence or a confirmed connector result can set; task completion alone leaves it Unconfirmed
      A: A11;A17: marking the task complete leaves the deliverable Unconfirmed; a filename-only link does not confirm it; reviewed evidence or a test-adapter confirmation sets it and records the source
   REQ-S04-002 [USER/SPECIFIED/final DG4] Make gates explicit approval records tied to a versioned, immutable evidence snapshot, never inferred from task completion
      P: Submitting a gate freezes the linked evidence record versions into a snapshot; approvers decide on that snapshot; completing all tasks never changes gate state
      A: A07;A08: completing every phase task leaves the gate Draft; editing a record after submission does not change the snapshot content shown to approvers

== separate delivery/adoption/value/closure
   REQ-PB-009 [SOURCE/SPECIFIED/final DG4] Apply 'Benefits before closure': an initiative is complete only when value is realized and sustained, not when delivered
      P: Initiatives carry separate delivery, value-realization and sustainment statuses; closure requires validated benefits and sustainment owner or a documented transition decision
      A: A11: an initiative with delivery=Complete and no validated benefit cannot be closed (API 409); UI shows 'Delivered — value validation pending'
   REQ-S03-003 [USER/SPECIFIED/final DG4] Keep initiative delivery, business adoption, validated value and transformation closure as separate statuses
      P: Each status has its own state machine and owner; none is derived from another; views show all four side by side
      A: A11: setting delivery to Complete leaves adoption, validated value and closure unchanged; the API rejects a closure request while validated value is pending unless a transition decision exists

== forecast never validated value
   REQ-PB-058 [SOURCE/SPECIFIED/final DG4] Prevent double counting: each benefit has a unique owner, baseline, formula and financial-statement or non-financial KPI link
      P: System rejects a benefit without a single owner, baseline, formula and a financial statement line or agreed non-financial KPI; initiatives link to canonical benefits via allocations, parent/child relationships and shared-benefit groups; portfolio totals sum canonical benefits, not links, so a shared benefit rolls up once
      A: A10: a benefit with two owners is rejected; a 10 million SAR benefit shared by two initiatives appears once (10 million SAR) in the portfolio total
   REQ-PB-076 [SOURCE/SPECIFIED/final DG4] Allow non-financial benefits with Value (SAR) n/a and Realized expressed as KPI actual
      P: For non-financial types (e.g. CX) Value (SAR) is n/a and Realized holds the KPI actual; no automatic monetization
      A: A10: a CX benefit saved with Value n/a is excluded from SAR totals and not counted as zero
   REQ-S08-001 [USER/SPECIFIED/final DG4] Track planned, forecast, measured, submitted-for-validation, validated, rejected and sustained benefit values separately
      P: Each benefit keeps separate value series per state; aggregations never combine states
      A: A10: a forecast amount never appears in the validated total; a rejected measurement is retained and shown as rejected
   REQ-S13-008 [USER/SPECIFIED/final DG5] Label provisional or unvalidated values clearly in reports and exports
      P: Values not validated carry a 'provisional' label
      A: A10;A15: a pending benefit value is labelled provisional in the PDF pack

== Finance validates, Business Owner accountable
   REQ-PB-012 [SOURCE/SPECIFIED/final DG2] Seed the six minimum governance roles with their source accountabilities and assign them per transformation
      P: Admin seeds roles; Transformation Lead/Office assign named people to roles per transformation; accountability text shown on the role assignment
      A: A12: a user assigned Workstream Lead on transformation X cannot read transformation Y; role accountability text matches B0018
   REQ-PB-013 [SOURCE/SPECIFIED/final DG4] Restrict Finance / Value Office validation of baseline, benefit logic and value realization to the Finance role
      P: Only users holding FIN on the transformation can mark a baseline, benefit formula or realized value as validated; others can submit for validation
      A: A10;A12: a Business Owner calling the validate endpoint receives 403; a Finance user succeeds and the audit event records validator identity
   REQ-PB-055 [SOURCE/SPECIFIED/final DG3] Require Finance validation of baseline and benefit logic early, before G4, not after delivery
      P: A business case cannot be submitted as G4 evidence until Finance has validated its baseline and benefit formulas
      A: A08;A10: G4 submission with a business case whose benefit formula is unvalidated is rejected listing 'Finance validation'
   REQ-PB-075 [SOURCE/SPECIFIED/final DG4] Implement Template 14 Benefits Register as a native register
      P: Users record benefits with Type (Revenue | Cost | CX | ...), Value (SAR) and Realized amounts, evidence source and Status R/A/G; IDs B01, B02...
      A: A10: T14 persists all 10 columns; realized value awaiting Finance validation is labelled pending and excluded from validated totals

== shared benefit once / allocation <=100% / unallocated
   REQ-PB-059 [SOURCE/SPECIFIED/final DG3] Record owners and capacity for mobilization
      P: Users record owners and capacity per initiative/wave; capacity shortfalls are shown for G4 and Wave 2 entry
      A: A01: a capacity demand exceeding availability shows a conflict indicator; G4 lists initiatives without owners
   REQ-S08-013 [USER/SPECIFIED/final DG4] Reject allocations over 100% and show any share below 100% as unallocated
      P: The server sums allocations per benefit; above 100% is rejected; below 100% shows the remaining share as unallocated
      A: A10: allocations 60% + 50% are rejected; 60% + 30% saves and shows 10% unallocated

== gates evidence-tied approvals
   REQ-PB-015 [SOURCE/SPECIFIED/final DG4] Model the six stage gates G1-G6 as explicit approval records with decision question and evidence required
      P: Owner assembles evidence, submits the gate; approver records decision against the evidence snapshot; gates are never inferred from task completion
      A: A08: submission with missing mandatory evidence is rejected; approval by a non-approver returns 403; approval of a stale submission version is rejected
   REQ-PB-016 [SOURCE/SPECIFIED/final DG2] G1 Case for Change: require diagnostic, baseline, root causes and value pools as gate evidence
      P: G1 checklist auto-links T01, baseline records and value pools; missing items block submission
      A: A08: G1 submission without any value pool record returns a validation error listing 'Value pools'
   REQ-S04-012 [USER/SPECIFIED/final DG4] Block gate submission when mandatory evidence is missing unless a specifically authorized exception is recorded
      P: Gate readiness is evaluated live and the gate page lists missing mandatory evidence; on submit the server checks each mandatory evidence item; missing items are listed and submission is refused unless an authorized, unexpired exception covers the item
      A: A08: the gate page lists missing items; submission with one missing mandatory item returns 422 listing it; with a valid exception it succeeds and the snapshot records the exception

== DG0-DG7 separate from G1-G6
   REQ-DLV-004 [ENGINEERING/IMPLEMENTED/final DG0] Define the ten project agents in .claude/agents with supported frontmatter, role instructions, handback contracts and verified loading and execution
      P: Orchestrator writes the ten definitions (transformation-analyst, solution-architect, frontend-ux-engineer, backend-workflow-engineer, kpi-benefits-engineer, devops-engineer, domain-reviewer, code-security-reviewer, qa-verifier, release-auditor), then invokes each through the runner to confirm it loads, runs and is write-guarded; the main session is the eleventh role, delivery-orchestrator
      A: A23: all ten definitions exist, and each has a recorded load run with a distinct session ID, a blocked out-of-scope write and a successful in-scope write (agents.md table)
   REQ-DLV-005 [ENGINEERING/SPECIFIED/final DG7] Apply each role's independence rule at every gate: no role reviews, certifies or approves its own work, and the orchestrator never records a review verdict
      P: For each gate the orchestrator assigns reviewers who authored nothing in the reviewed scope; each review record declares independence; the validator rejects a reviewer who is an implementation author or owner, or who shares an invocation with another reviewer
      A: A23: at every gate DG0-DG7 the validator accepts only review records whose reviewer_role is not in the gate's implementation authors and whose invocation references are distinct; the P0 test 'A23: a reviewer who authored the scope, or who is an owner, is rejected' passes

